## Part 1 · Enforce the layer’s memory policy

Make local cache memory bounded across arrivals while keeping all previous keys and values at global layers.

retention.py · append_packet(entries, keys, values, layer, window) — Return a new chronological list of [keys,values] entries after this token. Global layers retain all, local layers only the newest window. Do not mutate entries.

## Part 2 · Read shared KV heads

Implement a separate scaled softmax over retained token positions for each query head. A contiguous group shares keys and values but can produce different contexts.

grouped_read.py · read(queries, entries) — Return one value-width context per query head. Each cache entry is [K,V], each indexed by KV head. Consecutive equal-sized groups of query heads share one KV head.

## Run locally

Standard-library Python 3.10 or newer. Start at gateway.py to trace the model's entry point.

~~~sh
python run_lab.py fixtures/example_1.json
python -m unittest discover -s tests
~~~

